{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>And he said</b>. Then he said: \"This time I have found a helper corresponding to me, like me, for from me she was.\" And the matter of Lilith is a derashah." "<b>Because of this</b>. On account of this. And likewise: \"Say of me, he is my brother\" (Genesis 20:13)." "And the dagesh in the shin of \"אשה\" is in exchange for the hidden yud that is in \"איש\". And it is possible that the reason אשה is spoken with a dagesh and not rafeh is so that it not be confused with \"אישה\" meaning her husband, for sometimes the heh will be removed, and [there are] נשים from אנוש and אנשים." "And the meaning of יקרא על שֵם is:" "And the qof of לֻקָחָה זאת is not dagoshed, to lighten [it] for the tongue, though it is from the heavy binyan. And if it is not found" "And the meaning of והיו לבשר אחד is: as though they are, or that they resemble what they were. And there are those who say: they will give birth to another [n: read אחד]. And it is far-fetched."], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {4 "The phrase 'ואם לא נמצא' is left incomplete in the Hebrew; translated hyper-literally as 'and if it is not found,' with no continuation extant.", 5 "The text reads אחר ('another') but the parenthetical צ״ל אחד ('should read: one') indicates a suggested emendation to אחד ('one'), to match the singular 'one flesh.'"}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:43:24.812439331Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}